var e={"p ← the address of x":`p ← x 的地址`,"read the value at p        // 42":`读取 p 处的值        // 42`,"the value at p ← 7         // x is now 7":`p 处的值 ← 7         // x 现在是 7`,"p ← nothing":`p ← 空`,"Who holds what":`谁存着什么`,"Numbered cells":`带编号的格子`,"A computer’s memory is one long row of cells. Every cell has a number, its <strong>address</strong>, and can hold one value.":`计算机的内存是一长排格子。每个格子都有一个编号，即它的<strong>地址</strong>，并且能存放一个值。`,"Here are seven of them, at addresses 100 to 106. Real memory has billions.":`这里有七个，地址从 100 到 106。真实的内存有几十亿个。`,"A street of houses. The address tells you where; the house holds what.":`一条街上的房子。地址告诉你在哪里，房子里放着东西。`,"Nothing is stored yet.":`还什么都没存。`,"A variable is a named cell":`变量是有名字的格子`,Store:`存储`,"Writing <strong>x ← 42</strong> picks a free cell, puts 42 in it, and remembers that <em>x</em> means that cell.":`写下 <strong>x ← 42</strong>，就会选一个空闲的格子，把 42 放进去，并记住 <em>x</em> 指的就是这个格子。`,"You say x; the computer goes to address 102.":`你说 x，计算机就去地址 102。`,"The name is for you. The machine only ever uses the address.":`名字是给你看的。机器只用地址。`,"at 102":`在 102`,"A pointer holds an address":`指针存放地址`,Point:`指向`,"A cell can hold any number, and an address is a number. So a cell can hold the address of another cell.":`一个格子可以存放任何数字，而地址也是数字。所以一个格子可以存放另一个格子的地址。`,"That is a <strong>pointer</strong>. Here <em>p</em> lives at 105 and holds 102: it points at x.":`这就是<strong>指针</strong>。这里 <em>p</em> 位于 105，存放着 102：它指向 x。`,"“p knows where x is,” not “p is 42.”":`是“p 知道 x 在哪里”，而不是“p 是 42”。`,"at 105":`在 105`,"Follow the pointer":`沿着指针走`,"To use a pointer you <strong>follow</strong> it: read the address it holds, go to that cell, and take what is there.":`要使用指针，就要<strong>沿着</strong>它走：读出它存放的地址，去那个格子，取出那里的东西。`,"Following p leads to cell 102, which holds 42.":`沿着 p 走就到了格子 102，里面存着 42。`,"One extra hop. This is the hop a linked list makes for every node.":`多跳了一次。链表的每个节点都要这样跳一次。`,"value at p → 42":`p 处的值 → 42`,"Write through it":`通过它写入`,Write:`写入`,"You can also store through a pointer. Putting 7 “at p” goes to cell 102 and replaces what is there.":`你也可以通过指针存值。把 7 放到“p 处”，就会去格子 102，替换掉那里的内容。`,"Nobody mentioned x, but x is now 7. It is the same cell.":`没人提到 x，但 x 现在是 7 了。因为是同一个格子。`,"This is how one part of a program changes data another part thought was its own.":`程序的一部分就是这样改掉了另一部分以为属于自己的数据。`,"x is now 7":`x 现在是 7`,"Two pointers, one cell":`两个指针，一个格子`,Copy:`复制`,"Copying a pointer copies the <em>address</em>, not the thing it points at. <strong>q ← p</strong> gives q the number 102 too.":`复制指针复制的是<em>地址</em>，而不是它指向的东西。<strong>q ← p</strong> 让 q 也得到数字 102。`,"Now p and q both lead to the same cell. Change it through either and both see the change.":`现在 p 和 q 都通向同一个格子。通过任何一个修改它，两个都能看到变化。`,"at 100":`在 100`,"Pointing at nothing":`什么都不指向`,"A pointer does not have to point anywhere. A special value, usually called <strong>null</strong>, means “nothing”.":`指针不一定要指向某处。有一个特殊的值，通常叫 <strong>null</strong>，意思是“什么都没有”。`,"p is now null. q still points at x, and x is untouched.":`p 现在是 null。q 仍然指向 x，x 没有被动过。`,"Following a null pointer is an error. It is what ends a linked list.":`沿着空指针走是一个错误。链表的结尾就是它。`},t={"if n = 1:":`如果 n = 1:`,"return 1              // base case":`返回 1              // 基本情况`,"return n × fact(n − 1)    // smaller copy":`返回 n × fact(n − 1)    // 更小的副本`,"Who is waiting":`谁在等待`,"A function that calls itself":`调用自己的函数`,"The factorial of 4 is 4 × 3 × 2 × 1. But 3 × 2 × 1 is the factorial of 3, so <strong>fact(4) = 4 × fact(3)</strong>: the problem contains a smaller copy of itself.":`4 的阶乘是 4 × 3 × 2 × 1。但 3 × 2 × 1 是 3 的阶乘，所以 <strong>fact(4) = 4 × fact(3)</strong>：问题里包含着一个更小的自己。`,"A function written that way is <strong>recursive</strong>. Calling it puts a <em>frame</em> on the call stack: its notes while it runs.":`这样写的函数是<strong>递归</strong>的。调用它会在调用栈上放一个<em>栈帧</em>：它运行时的笔记。`,"Asking a question whose answer needs the same question, about something smaller.":`提一个问题，而它的答案需要对更小的东西提同一个问题。`,"needs fact(3)":`需要 fact(3)`,Running:`运行中`,nobody:`无`,"Frames on the stack":`栈上的栈帧`,"Calls pile up":`调用越叠越高`,Call:`调用`,"fact(4) cannot finish until it knows fact(3), so it calls it and waits. fact(3) needs fact(2), which needs fact(1).":`fact(4) 要知道 fact(3) 才能完成，所以它调用 fact(3) 并等待。fact(3) 需要 fact(2)，fact(2) 又需要 fact(1)。`,"Every call adds a frame on top. Nothing has been multiplied yet: the stack is only remembering who is waiting for whom.":`每次调用都在顶上加一个栈帧。还什么都没乘：栈只是记着谁在等谁。`,"needs fact(2)":`需要 fact(2)`,"needs fact(1)":`需要 fact(1)`,"The base case":`基本情况`,"fact(1) is different. It does not need another call: the answer is simply 1.":`fact(1) 不一样。它不需要再调用别的：答案就是 1。`,"This is the <strong>base case</strong>, an input small enough to answer directly. It is where the pile stops growing.":`这就是<strong>基本情况</strong>：一个小到可以直接回答的输入。栈就是在这里停止增长的。`,"Every recursion needs a base case, and every call must move towards it.":`每个递归都需要基本情况，而且每次调用都必须朝它靠近。`,"returns 1":`返回 1`,"Handing the answer back":`把答案交回去`,Return:`返回`,"fact(1) returns 1 and its frame comes off the stack. That 1 is exactly what fact(2) was waiting for.":`fact(1) 返回 1，它的栈帧从栈上移除。这个 1 正是 fact(2) 在等的。`,"Now fact(2) can do its own small job: 2 × 1 = 2.":`现在 fact(2) 可以做自己的小工作了：2 × 1 = 2。`,Unwinding:`展开`,"The same thing happens one frame down. fact(2) returns 2, and fact(3) finishes: 3 × 2 = 6.":`往下一帧也是同样的过程。fact(2) 返回 2，fact(3) 完成：3 × 2 = 6。`,"The calls went up the stack; the answers come back down it, in the opposite order.":`调用沿着栈往上走；答案按相反的顺序沿着栈往下回来。`,"Last called, first finished. The call stack is a stack.":`最后调用的，最先完成。调用栈就是一个栈。`,"The answer":`答案`,"fact(3) returns 6 to the first call, which has been waiting all this time: 4 × 6 = <strong>24</strong>.":`fact(3) 把 6 返回给第一次调用，它一直在等：4 × 6 = <strong>24</strong>。`,"Four calls, four frames. Recursion uses memory in proportion to how deep it goes.":`四次调用，四个栈帧。递归占用的内存与它的深度成正比。`,"Without a base case":`没有基本情况`,"Take the base case away and fact(1) calls fact(0), which calls fact(−1), and on, and on. No call ever returns.":`去掉基本情况，fact(1) 就会调用 fact(0)，fact(0) 又调用 fact(−1)，没完没了。没有一次调用会返回。`,"Each one still needs a frame, and the stack has only so much room. When it runs out, the program stops: a <strong>stack overflow</strong>.":`每次调用仍然需要一个栈帧，而栈的空间是有限的。空间用完时，程序就会停止：这就是<strong>栈溢出</strong>。`,"Deep recursion can overflow even with a base case. A loop uses one frame, however long it runs.":`即使有基本情况，太深的递归也会溢出。循环无论运行多久，都只用一个栈帧。`,"stack overflow":`栈溢出`,"More frames than the stack has room for.":`栈帧多到栈装不下。`},n={"return a[i]":`返回 a[i]`,"for each item from the last down to i:":`对每个 项，从最后一项到第 i 项:`,"move it one cell right":`把它右移一格`,"for each item after i, from left to right:":`对每个 i 之后的项，从左到右:`,"move it one cell left":`把它左移一格`,"put x in the first free cell":`把 x 放进第一个空格子`,"Cells in a row":`一排格子`,"An array is one block of memory cut into equal cells, numbered from 0. The values sit side by side, in order, with no gaps.":`数组是一整块内存，切成大小相同的格子，从 0 开始编号。值一个挨一个按顺序排着，中间没有空隙。`,"This one has room for seven values and is holding five. Call it <strong>a</strong>.":`这个数组能放七个值，现在放了五个。叫它 <strong>a</strong>。`,"A row of numbered lockers, all the same size.":`一排带编号的储物柜，大小都一样。`,"Jump straight there":`直接跳过去`,"Because every cell is the same size, the computer can work out where cell 3 is: the start of the array, plus three cells along.":`因为每个格子大小相同，计算机可以算出格子 3 在哪里：数组的起点，再往后数三个格子。`,"So it goes straight there. It does not visit cells 0, 1 and 2 on the way, however long the array is.":`所以它直接跳过去。不管数组多长，它都不会顺路经过格子 0、1 和 2。`,"O(1). A linked list would have to hop there node by node.":`O(1)。链表就得一个节点一个节点地跳过去。`,"To put 15 at index 2, cell 2 has to be empty first. So 31, 25 and 19 each move one cell to the right, starting from the end.":`要把 15 放到下标 2，格子 2 必须先空出来。所以 31、25 和 19 从末尾开始，各自右移一格。`,"Only then can 15 go in.":`然后 15 才能放进去。`,"O(n): the nearer the front you insert, the more there is to move.":`O(n)：插入的位置越靠前，要移动的就越多。`,"Taking 12 out leaves a hole at index 1, and an array may not have holes.":`拿掉 12 会在下标 1 留下一个洞，而数组不能有洞。`,"So everything after it moves one cell to the left to close the gap.":`所以它后面的所有值都左移一格，把空隙填上。`,"O(n) again: four values moved to remove one.":`又是 O(n)：为了删一个值，移动了四个。`,"Adding at the end is the cheap case. 40 goes into the first free cell, and nothing else has to move.":`在末尾添加是便宜的情况。40 放进第一个空格子，其他什么都不用动。`,"O(1), as long as there is a free cell.":`O(1)，只要还有空格子。`,"When it is full":`满了怎么办`,"Add 52 and every cell is used. An array cannot grow where it stands: the memory just past it belongs to something else.":`再加 52，所有格子就都用上了。数组不能原地变大：紧挨着它的内存属于别的东西。`,"To hold more you need a bigger array, and to copy everything across. A dynamic array does that for you.":`要放更多，你需要一个更大的数组，并把所有东西复制过去。动态数组会替你做这件事。`,"Lots of “give me item i”: array. Lots of inserting in the middle: linked list.":`经常“给我第 i 项”：用数组。经常在中间插入：用链表。`},r={"table ← for each beginning of pattern, the length of":`table ← 对模式的每个开头部分，记下`,"its longest start, short of the whole, that is also its end":`它最长的、不是整体的、同时也是结尾的开头的长度`,"m ← 0                          // letters matched so far":`m ← 0                          // 已匹配的字母数`,"for each letter c of text:":`对每个 文本中的字母 c:`,"while m > 0 and c ≠ pattern[m]:":`当 m > 0 且 c ≠ pattern[m]:`,"m ← table[m − 1]       // fall back, re-read nothing":`m ← table[m − 1]       // 回退，不重读任何东西`,"if c = pattern[m]: m ← m + 1":`如果 c = pattern[m]: m ← m + 1`,"if m = length of pattern: return found":`如果 m = 模式的长度: 返回 找到`,"Never look twice":`永不看两遍`,"The simple search found A B A C in this text with nine comparisons. Each time it failed it moved along one place and started the pattern again from its first letter, re-reading text it had already seen.":`简单的搜索用了九次比较，才在这段文本里找到 A B A C。每次失败，它都右移一位，再从第一个字母重新开始模式，重读已经看过的文本。`,"The <strong>Knuth–Morris–Pratt</strong> search, KMP, reads each letter of the text once and never goes back.":`<strong>Knuth–Morris–Pratt</strong> 搜索，即 KMP，文本的每个字母只读一次，从不回头。`,"Fallback table":`回退表`,"for A, AB, ABA, ABAC":`对应 A、AB、ABA、ABAC`,"Three match, then a miss":`三个匹配，然后失配`,"It begins the same way. A, B, A all match. The fourth letter does not: the pattern wants C and the text has B.":`开头一样。A、B、A 都匹配。第四个字母不匹配：模式要 C，文本是 B。`,"The simple search would now throw those three matches away.":`简单的搜索这时会把这三个匹配全扔掉。`,"What the matches already say":`匹配已经告诉了你什么`,"Three letters matched, so the text there is known to be A B A, without looking at it again. Could a match start one place along? It would need B to equal A. No.":`三个字母匹配了，所以不用再看就知道那里的文本是 A B A。匹配能从后一位开始吗？那需要 B 等于 A。不行。`,"Two places along? It would need A to equal A. Yes. That works because the matched part <strong>ends the way it begins</strong>: with an A.":`后两位呢？那需要 A 等于 A。可以。之所以可行，是因为匹配的部分<strong>结尾和开头一样</strong>：都是 A。`,"starts and ends with A":`以 A 开头，也以 A 结尾`,"ABA: its longest start that is also its end has length 1.":`ABA：既是开头又是结尾的最长部分，长度为 1。`,"Slide so they line up":`滑动到对齐`,"So slide the pattern two places, putting its first A under the A that ended the match. That letter is already known to match. It is not compared again.":`所以把模式滑两位，让它的第一个 A 对准结束匹配的那个 A。已知那个字母是匹配的，不再比较。`,"One of the pattern’s letters is accounted for before a single new comparison is made.":`还没做一次新的比较，模式就有一个字母已经确定了。`,"known: no need to look":`已知：不用看`,"Carry on from where the text stopped":`从文本停下的地方继续`,"The text was at its fourth letter, and it stays there. Compare it with the pattern’s second letter: B = B. Then A = A, then C = C.":`文本停在第四个字母，现在也还在那里。把它和模式的第二个字母比较：B = B。然后 A = A，然后 C = C。`,"Found at place 2 with seven comparisons instead of nine, and no letter of the text read twice.":`在位置 2 找到，七次比较而不是九次，文本中没有一个字母读了两遍。`,"The table that makes it work":`让它运转的那张表`,"How far to fall back depends only on the pattern, so it is worked out once, before the search. For every beginning of the pattern, note the length of its longest start that is also its end: A is 0, AB is 0, ABA is 1, ABAC is 0.":`回退多远只取决于模式，所以在搜索之前算一次就行。对模式的每个开头部分，记下它既是开头又是结尾的最长部分的长度：A 是 0，AB 是 0，ABA 是 1，ABAC 是 0。`,"After a miss with m letters matched, keep table[m − 1] of them and carry on.":`匹配了 m 个字母后失配，就保留其中 table[m − 1] 个，继续往下。`,"O(n + m) for a text of n letters and a pattern of m. The simple search is O(n × m) at worst.":`文本 n 个字母、模式 m 个字母时是 O(n + m)。简单的搜索最坏是 O(n × m)。`},i={"Finding a cell":`找一个格子`,"Rows and columns":`行与列`,"An array has one index. A <strong>matrix</strong>, or 2D array, has two: a row and a column. Images, game boards, spreadsheets and maps are all stored this way.":`数组有一个下标。<strong>矩阵</strong>，也就是二维数组，有两个：行和列。图片、棋盘、电子表格和地图都是这样存储的。`,"This one has 3 rows and 4 columns: twelve cells.":`这个矩阵有 3 行 4 列：十二个格子。`,"3 rows × 4 columns":`3 行 × 4 列`,Cell:`格子`,"Place in memory":`在内存中的位置`,"row × 4 + column":`行 × 4 + 列`,"Two numbers find a cell":`两个数确定一个格子`,Access:`访问`,"Give a row and a column and you have the cell: row 1, column 2. As with a plain array, nothing is searched. It is still O(1).":`给出行和列，就得到了格子：第 1 行，第 2 列。和普通数组一样，不需要搜索。仍然是 O(1)。`,"row 1, column 2":`第 1 行，第 2 列`,"Really one long row":`其实是一长排`,"Memory has no second dimension. The rows are simply laid end to end: row 0, then row 1, then row 2.":`内存没有第二个维度。各行只是首尾相接地排着：第 0 行，然后第 1 行，然后第 2 行。`,"So a cell’s real position is <strong>row × width + column</strong>. Row 1, column 2 is at 1 × 4 + 2 = 6, which is the number written on it.":`所以一个格子真正的位置是<strong>行 × 宽度 + 列</strong>。第 1 行第 2 列位于 1 × 4 + 2 = 6，正是写在它上面的数字。`,"row 1 is 4 to 7":`第 1 行是 4 到 7`,"The number in each cell is its place in memory.":`每个格子里的数字是它在内存中的位置。`,"Which way you walk matters":`走的方向很重要`,"Walking along a row visits cells that sit side by side in memory. Walking down a column jumps four places each time.":`沿着一行走，访问的格子在内存中是挨着的。沿着一列往下走，每次都要跳四个位置。`,"Both visit every cell, but on a large matrix the row-by-row walk can be several times faster, because computers read memory in neighbouring chunks.":`两种走法都会访问每个格子，但在大矩阵上，一行一行地走可能快好几倍，因为计算机是一块一块地读取相邻内存的。`,"Loop over rows on the outside, columns on the inside.":`外层循环遍历行，内层循环遍历列。`,"every fourth cell":`每隔四个格子`,"column 2":`第 2 列`,"A cell’s neighbours are one step away in each direction: up, down, left, right. Add or subtract 1 from the row or the column.":`一个格子的邻居在每个方向上都只差一步：上、下、左、右。把行或列加 1 或减 1 即可。`,"That turns a grid into a graph without storing a single edge, which is how mazes, flood fills and many dynamic-programming tables are handled.":`这样不用存一条边，就把网格变成了图，迷宫、泛洪填充和许多动态规划表格都是这样处理的。`,"four neighbours":`四个邻居`,"Check the edges: corner cells have only two.":`注意边缘：角上的格子只有两个邻居。`},a={"put x on top":`把 x 放到顶上`,"if the stack is empty: error":`如果 栈为空: 错误`,"take the top item off":`把顶上的项拿走`,"return the top item, leaving it there":`返回 顶上的项，并把它留在原处`,"return whether nothing is left":`返回 是否什么都没剩下`,"What is a stack?":`栈是什么？`,"A stack is a pile. You can add to the top and take from the top, and that is all.":`栈就是一摞东西。你只能往顶上放，从顶上拿，仅此而已。`,"So the last item you put on is the first one you get back: <strong>LIFO</strong>, last in, first out.":`所以你最后放上去的，就是你最先拿回来的：<strong>LIFO</strong>，后进先出。`,"A pile of plates. Nobody pulls one out from the middle.":`一摞盘子。没人会从中间抽出一个。`,"<strong>push(x)</strong> puts a new item on top. Here 40 leaves the input tray and lands on the pile.":`<strong>push(x)</strong> 把一个新项放到顶上。这里 40 离开输入托盘，落到这一摞上。`,"Nothing underneath has to move, so a push costs the same whether the stack holds three items or three million.":`下面的东西都不用动，所以不管栈里有三个项还是三百万个，一次 push 的代价都一样。`,"O(1): one step, however tall the stack is.":`O(1)：一步，不管栈有多高。`,Top:`栈顶`,"<strong>top()</strong> tells you what is on top without taking it off. You will also see it called <em>peek</em>.":`<strong>top()</strong> 告诉你顶上是什么，但不把它拿走。你也会看到它叫 <em>peek</em>。`,"The stack is exactly as it was afterwards.":`之后栈和原来一模一样。`,"O(1): the top is always in the same place.":`O(1)：栈顶总在同一个地方。`,"<strong>pop()</strong> removes the top item and hands it back. It is the only way to take anything out of a stack.":`<strong>pop()</strong> 拿走顶上的项并把它交给你。这是从栈里取出东西的唯一方法。`,"40 was the last block in, so it is the first one out.":`40 是最后放进去的方块，所以它最先出来。`,"Popping an empty stack is an error. Check empty() first.":`对空栈执行 pop 是一个错误。先检查 empty()。`,"Last in, first out":`后进先出`,"Pop again and 30 comes out. The blocks went in as 10, 20, 30, 40 and they are leaving as 40, 30, …":`再 pop 一次，30 出来了。方块按 10、20、30、40 进去，现在按 40、30、…… 出来。`,"A stack always gives things back in the reverse of the order they arrived.":`栈总是按到达顺序的相反顺序把东西还给你。`,"To reach 10 at the bottom, everything above it has to come off first.":`要拿到底部的 10，上面的所有东西都得先拿走。`,"Each time a function calls another, the computer pushes a frame onto the <strong>call stack</strong>. When the function returns, its frame is popped and the caller carries on.":`每当一个函数调用另一个函数，计算机就往<strong>调用栈</strong>上压入一个栈帧。函数返回时，它的栈帧被弹出，调用者继续执行。`,"Undo history and the browser’s Back button work the same way.":`撤销历史和浏览器的“后退”按钮也是这样工作的。`,"“Stack overflow” is this stack running out of room, usually from recursion that never stops.":`“栈溢出”就是这个栈空间用完了，通常是因为递归停不下来。`},o={"put x at the rear":`把 x 放到队尾`,"if the queue is empty: error":`如果 队列为空: 错误`,"take the front item off":`把队首的项拿走`,"return the front item, leaving it there":`返回 队首的项，并把它留在原处`,"What is a queue?":`队列是什么？`,"A queue is a line. You join at the back and you leave from the front, and nobody jumps ahead.":`队列就是排队。你从队尾加入，从队首离开，谁也不能插队。`,"So the first item in is the first one out: <strong>FIFO</strong>, first in, first out.":`所以最先进去的就是最先出来的：<strong>FIFO</strong>，先进先出。`,"The line at a checkout. Whoever has waited longest is served next.":`收银台前的队伍。等得最久的人下一个被服务。`,"<strong>enqueue(x)</strong> adds a new item at the <strong>rear</strong>. Here 40 leaves the input tray and joins the back of the line.":`<strong>enqueue(x)</strong> 在<strong>队尾</strong>加入一个新项。这里 40 离开输入托盘，排到了队伍末尾。`,"Nobody already waiting has to move.":`已经在等的人都不用动。`,"O(1): one step, however long the line is.":`O(1)：一步，不管队伍有多长。`,Front:`队首`,"<strong>front()</strong> tells you who is next without taking them out of the line. You will also see it called <em>peek</em>.":`<strong>front()</strong> 告诉你下一个是谁，但不把它从队伍里拿出来。你也会看到它叫 <em>peek</em>。`,"The queue is exactly as it was afterwards.":`之后队列和原来一模一样。`,"O(1): the front is always in the same place.":`O(1)：队首总在同一个地方。`,"<strong>dequeue()</strong> removes the item at the <strong>front</strong> and hands it back. 10 has waited longest, so 10 goes.":`<strong>dequeue()</strong> 移除<strong>队首</strong>的项并把它交给你。10 等得最久，所以 10 离开。`,"Everyone behind moves up one place, and 20 is now at the front.":`后面的每个人都往前挪一位，现在 20 在队首。`,"Dequeuing from an empty queue is an error.":`对空队列执行 dequeue 是一个错误。`,"First in, first out":`先进先出`,"Dequeue again and 20 comes out. They joined as 10, 20, 30, 40 and they are leaving as 10, 20, …":`再 dequeue 一次，20 出来了。它们按 10、20、30、40 加入，现在按 10、20、…… 离开。`,"A queue gives things back in exactly the order they arrived. A stack gives them back in reverse.":`队列按到达的顺序原样把东西还给你。栈则是倒过来还。`,"You add at one end and remove at the other. A stack does both at the same end.":`你在一端添加，在另一端移除。栈两件事都在同一端做。`,"Whenever work arrives faster than it can be done, it waits in a queue. Send three files to a printer and they come out in the order you sent them.":`只要工作来得比做得快，它就会在队列里等着。给打印机发三个文件，它们会按你发送的顺序打印出来。`,"Requests to a web server, keys you have typed, messages between programs: all queued.":`发往网页服务器的请求、你敲下的按键、程序之间的消息：全都在排队。`,"Exploring a maze level by level, or a graph breadth-first, also runs on a queue.":`一层一层地探索迷宫，或者广度优先地遍历图，也都靠队列。`},s={"put x at the front":`把 x 放到前端`,"put x at the back":`把 x 放到后端`,"take the front item off, return it":`把前端的项拿走并返回它`,"take the back item off, return it":`把后端的项拿走并返回它`,"put every letter in a deque":`把每个字母放进一个双端队列`,"while more than one is left:":`当 剩下的不止一个:`,"if pop_front() ≠ pop_back(): return no":`如果 pop_front() ≠ pop_back(): 返回 否`,"return yes":`返回 是`,"Open at both ends":`两端都开口`,"A stack lets you in and out at one end. A queue lets you in at one end and out at the other. A <strong>deque</strong> (say “deck”) is a double-ended queue: you can add or remove at <em>either</em> end.":`栈让你在一端进出。队列让你从一端进、从另一端出。<strong>双端队列</strong>（deque）是两头都能用的队列：你可以在<em>任意一端</em>添加或移除。`,"It has a front and a back, and a way in and out at each.":`它有前端和后端，每一端都可以进出。`,"A train: carriages can be coupled or uncoupled at either end, never in the middle.":`一列火车：车厢可以在任意一端挂上或摘下，从不在中间。`,"Nothing in the middle is ever touched.":`中间的东西从来不会被碰到。`,"<strong>push_back(10)</strong> adds at the back. 10 becomes the new back; nothing else moves.":`<strong>push_back(10)</strong> 在后端添加。10 成为新的后端；其他什么都不动。`,"So far this is just a queue’s enqueue.":`到目前为止，这只是队列的入队。`,"<strong>push_front(50)</strong> adds at the other end, in front of everything.":`<strong>push_front(50)</strong> 在另一端添加，排在所有东西前面。`,"A queue cannot do this: nobody is allowed to join at the front of a line.":`队列做不到这一点：谁都不许插到队伍最前面。`,"<strong>pop_front()</strong> takes the front item off and hands it back.":`<strong>pop_front()</strong> 把前端的项拿走并交给你。`,"50 went in at the front and came straight back out of it. Use only this end and a deque behaves as a <strong>stack</strong>.":`50 从前端进去，又直接从前端出来。只用这一端的话，双端队列就像一个<strong>栈</strong>。`,"In and out at one end: last in, first out.":`在同一端进出：后进先出。`,"<strong>pop_back()</strong> takes from the back instead.":`<strong>pop_back()</strong> 则从后端取。`,"Push at one end and pop at the other and it is a <strong>queue</strong>. A deque is both, and every one of its four operations is O(1).":`在一端压入、在另一端弹出，它就是一个<strong>队列</strong>。双端队列两者兼备，而且四种操作都是 O(1)。`,"Only the ends change, so the length of the deque never matters.":`只有两端会变，所以双端队列有多长都无所谓。`,"In at one end, out at the other: first in, first out.":`一端进，另一端出：先进先出。`,"Using both ends":`两端一起用`,Example:`例子`,"Some jobs need both ends at once. Is LEVEL a <strong>palindrome</strong>, a word that reads the same backwards?":`有些工作需要同时用两端。LEVEL 是<strong>回文</strong>吗？也就是倒着读也一样的词？`,"Put its letters in a deque. If it is one, the letter at the front must always match the letter at the back.":`把它的字母放进双端队列。如果它是回文，前端的字母必须总是和后端的字母一样。`,"From the front":`从前端`,"From the back":`从后端`,"Letters left":`剩下的字母`,"Compare the ends":`比较两端`,"Pop one letter from each end and compare them. L and L: they match, so carry on with what is left.":`从两端各弹出一个字母，比较它们。L 和 L：一样，所以继续处理剩下的。`,"Neither pop had to search for anything. Each took one step.":`两次弹出都不需要搜索。每次只用一步。`,"They match.":`一样。`,"Until one is left":`直到只剩一个`,"Again: E and E. They match too. One letter is left, and a single letter has nothing to disagree with.":`再来：E 和 E。也一样。只剩一个字母，单个字母没有什么可以不一样的。`,"LEVEL is a palindrome, found by working inwards from both ends.":`LEVEL 是回文，这是从两端往中间推算出来的。`,"Undo histories with a size limit, sliding-window maximums, schedulers that take work from either end.":`有长度上限的撤销历史、滑动窗口最大值、从任意一端取任务的调度器。`,"LEVEL is a palindrome.":`LEVEL 是回文。`},c={"big-o":{"return a[0]":`返回 a[0]`,"repeat: look at the middle, keep one half":`重复: 看中间，留下一半`,"for each item in a:":`对每个 a 中的项:`,"add it on":`把它加上`,"for each other item in a:":`对每个 a 中的其他项:`,"compare the two":`比较这两项`,"Steps taken":`所用步数`,"Count steps, not seconds":`数步数，不数秒数`,"How fast is an algorithm? Seconds depend on the machine. So instead we count <strong>steps</strong>, and ask how that count depends on the size of the input, <em>n</em>.":`一个算法有多快？秒数取决于机器。所以我们改为数<strong>步数</strong>，并且问：这个数字如何随输入规模 <em>n</em> 变化。`,"Here are four kinds of algorithm working on 2 items. Each block is one step of work. They look much the same.":`这里有四种算法，各自处理 2 个项。每个方块是一步工作。它们看起来差不多。`,"On small inputs almost anything is fast. The differences show when n grows.":`输入很小的时候，几乎什么都快。n 变大时，差别才显现出来。`,constant:`常数`,logarithmic:`对数`,linear:`线性`,quadratic:`平方`,"Steps for n = 2 items.":`n = 2 个项时的步数。`,"Double the input":`输入翻倍`,"Give them 4 items instead of 2. One platform has not changed. One gained a single block. One doubled. One is four times the size.":`给它们 4 个项，而不是 2 个。一个平台没有变化。一个多了一个方块。一个翻了一倍。一个变成了四倍大。`,"That reaction to growth is what Big-O describes.":`这种对增长的反应，正是大 O 所描述的。`,"Steps for n = 4 items.":`n = 4 个项时的步数。`,"Double it again":`再翻一倍`,"8 items. The same thing happens again, each growing in its own way: not at all, by one, by double, by four times.":`8 个项。同样的事情再次发生，每个都按自己的方式增长：完全不变、多一步、翻倍、变成四倍。`,"Big-O names the <strong>shape of the growth</strong>, and ignores the details. 2n steps and n + 5 steps are both just O(n).":`大 O 说的是<strong>增长的形状</strong>，忽略细节。2n 步和 n + 5 步都只是 O(n)。`,"“O(n)” is “the work grows in step with n.”":`“O(n)”的意思是“工作量随 n 同步增长”。`,"Steps for n = 8 items.":`n = 8 个项时的步数。`,"O(1): constant":`O(1)：常数`,Constant:`常数`,"The work does not depend on n at all. Reading an array cell by its index, pushing onto a stack: one step, for 8 items or 8 million.":`工作量完全不取决于 n。按下标读取数组的一个格子、往栈里压入一个值：一步，不管是 8 个项还是 800 万个。`,"This is as good as it gets.":`没有比这更好的了。`,"O(log n): logarithmic":`O(log n)：对数`,Logarithmic:`对数`,"Each step throws away half of what is left, as binary search does. Doubling the input adds just <strong>one</strong> more step.":`每一步都扔掉剩下的一半，就像二分查找那样。输入翻倍，只多<strong>一</strong>步。`,"A million items take about 20 steps. A billion take about 30.":`一百万个项大约需要 20 步。十亿个大约需要 30 步。`,"O(n): linear":`O(n)：线性`,Linear:`线性`,"Every item is looked at once: adding up a list, or searching one that is not sorted. Twice the input, twice the work.":`每个项都看一次：把一个列表加起来，或者在没排序的列表里搜索。输入翻倍，工作量也翻倍。`,"Often this is the best possible, because you cannot skip items you have never seen.":`这往往已经是最好的了，因为你没法跳过从没看过的项。`,"O(n²): quadratic":`O(n²)：平方`,Quadratic:`平方`,"Every item is compared with every other: a loop inside a loop. Twice the input, <strong>four times</strong> the work.":`每个项都要和其他每个项比较：循环里套循环。输入翻倍，工作量变成<strong>四倍</strong>。`,"Fine for 8 items. For a million it is a trillion steps, and it is usually the first thing worth fixing.":`8 个项没问题。一百万个就是一万亿步，这通常是第一个值得优化的地方。`,"Much of this course is turning an O(n²) idea into O(n) or O(n log n).":`这门课的很多内容，就是把 O(n²) 的思路变成 O(n) 或 O(n log n)。`},memory:e,recursion:t,"divide-and-conquer":{"if problem is small enough:":`如果 问题足够小:`,"return its answer directly       // base case":`返回 直接给出的答案       // 基本情况`,"split problem into smaller pieces    // divide":`把问题拆成更小的部分    // 分`,"solve each piece the same way        // conquer":`用同样的方法解决每个部分        // 治`,"return their answers, put together   // combine":`返回 拼在一起的各部分答案   // 合`,"The shape of the work":`工作的形状`,"Too big to do at once":`太大，没法一次做完`,"Some problems are hard at full size and easy when they are tiny. Sorting eight cards takes thought. Sorting one card takes none.":`有些问题在完整规模时很难，变得很小时就很容易。给八张牌排序要动脑子，给一张牌排序完全不用。`,"<strong>Divide and conquer</strong> is a recipe for getting from the first to the second: split the problem, solve the pieces, and join their answers.":`<strong>分治</strong>是从前者走到后者的方法：拆分问题，解决各部分，再合并它们的答案。`,"a problem of size 8":`规模为 8 的问题`,"Pieces at the bottom":`底层的部分`,"Size of each":`每部分的大小`,Levels:`层数`,"Cut the problem into smaller problems of the same kind. Most often that means in half: two problems of size 4.":`把问题切成同类的更小问题。最常见的是对半切：两个规模为 4 的问题。`,"Nothing has been solved yet. But each half can now be handled by the very same method, which is where recursion comes in.":`还什么都没解决。但现在每一半都可以用完全相同的方法处理，这就是递归登场的地方。`,"Until it is trivial":`直到变得微不足道`,"Each half is halved again, and again, until the pieces cannot get smaller. A piece of size 1 needs no work: that is the <strong>base case</strong>.":`每一半再对半切，一次又一次，直到不能再小。规模为 1 的部分不需要任何工作：这就是<strong>基本情况</strong>。`,"Halving 8 reaches 1 in three cuts. Halving n takes log n.":`8 对半切三次就到 1。n 对半切需要 log n 次。`,"Combine on the way back":`在返回的路上合并`,"Now the answers travel upward. Two solved pieces are joined into the answer for the piece above them, and so on to the top.":`现在答案向上传递。两个已解决的部分合并成它们上一层部分的答案，一直到顶。`,"The numbers show the order pieces are finished in. Both halves are always done before the whole they belong to.":`数字表示各部分完成的顺序。两半总是在它们所属的整体之前完成。`,"In merge sort, this joining is the merge.":`在归并排序里，这个合并就是归并。`,"Add it up level by level":`一层一层地加起来`,"How much work is that? Look across each level. However the 8 is cut up, the sizes on one level still add up to 8.":`这一共要多少工作？横着看每一层。不管 8 怎么切，同一层的大小加起来仍然是 8。`,"If joining takes time in proportion to the size of the piece, as merging does, every level costs n. There are log n + 1 levels, so the total is about n log n.":`如果合并所需的时间与部分的大小成正比，就像归并那样，那么每层的代价是 n。一共有 log n + 1 层，所以总量大约是 n log n。`,"Depth 0":`深度 0`,"Depth 1":`深度 1`,"Depth 2":`深度 2`,"Depth 3":`深度 3`,Total:`总计`,"4 levels × 8 = 32":`4 层 × 8 = 32`,"Or follow only one branch":`或者只走一个分支`,Variation:`变体`,"Some methods split the problem and then need only <em>one</em> of the pieces. Binary search looks at the middle and throws the other half away.":`有些方法拆分问题后只需要其中<em>一个</em>部分。二分查找看一眼中间，就把另一半扔掉。`,"Then the work is one piece per level: log n in all. Counting pieces per level and work per piece is how every cost of this kind is found.":`那么每层只有一个部分的工作量：总共 log n。数清每层有几个部分、每个部分要多少工作，这类代价都是这样算出来的。`,"Merge sort":`归并排序`,"both halves, n to join: n log n":`两半都要，合并要 n：n log n`,"Binary search":`二分查找`,"one half, 1 to choose: log n":`只要一半，选择要 1：log n`,"one part, n to split: about n":`只要一部分，拆分要 n：大约 n`,"When it fits":`什么时候适用`,"It works when the pieces are <strong>independent</strong>: solving one tells you nothing about another. Merge sort, quick sort, binary search and quickselect are all this recipe.":`当各部分<strong>相互独立</strong>时，它就适用：解决一个部分不会告诉你任何关于另一个部分的事。归并排序、快速排序、二分查找和快速选择都是这个方法。`,"When the same small piece keeps turning up inside different big ones, solving it afresh each time is wasteful. That is the sign to switch to dynamic programming.":`如果同一个小部分在不同的大部分里反复出现，每次都重新解决它就是浪费。这就是该换成动态规划的信号。`,"The four strategies":`四种策略`,"Divide and conquer, greedy, backtracking and dynamic programming. Most algorithms in this course are one of them.":`分治、贪心、回溯和动态规划。这门课里的大多数算法都属于其中之一。`},arrays:n,"dynamic-arrays":{"if size = capacity:":`如果 size = capacity:`,"make a new array, twice as big":`新建一个两倍大的数组`,"for each item:":`对每个 项:`,"move it across":`把它搬过去`,"let the old array go":`释放旧数组`,"Size and capacity":`大小与容量`,"A fixed number of cells":`固定数量的格子`,"An array is given its cells when it is made, and it cannot be given more later: the memory after it may already belong to something else.":`数组在创建时得到它的格子，之后不能再多给：紧挨着它的内存可能已经属于别的东西了。`,"This one has room for three. Two are in use. That is its <strong>size</strong> (2) and its <strong>capacity</strong> (3).":`这个数组能放三个。用了两个。这就是它的<strong>大小</strong>（2）和<strong>容量</strong>（3）。`,"How do lists that “just grow” work, if arrays cannot?":`既然数组不能变大，那些“自己会长”的列表是怎么做到的？`,"of 3":`/ 3`,"Appends so far":`已追加次数`,"Items moved":`已移动项数`,"Append, while there is room":`有空位时追加`,"Adding at the end is easy when a cell is free: put the value in the next one and count it.":`有空格子时，在末尾添加很容易：把值放进下一个格子，然后计数加一。`,"13 goes into cell 2. Nothing else has to move, so it is O(1). But now the array is full.":`13 放进格子 2。其他什么都不用动，所以是 O(1)。但现在数组满了。`,"No room":`没有空位`,"Now append 21. There is no cell 3: the array ends at cell 2, and it cannot be stretched.":`现在追加 21。没有格子 3：数组在格子 2 就结束了，而且不能拉长。`,"The value has nowhere to go.":`这个值无处可放。`,"Size equals capacity: time to grow.":`大小等于容量：该扩容了。`,"Make a bigger one":`造一个更大的`,"The way out is to ask for a whole new array, somewhere there <em>is</em> room.":`出路是申请一个全新的数组，放在<em>有</em>空间的地方。`,"Not one cell bigger: <strong>twice as big</strong>. That choice is what makes this cheap, as you will see.":`不是只大一格，而是<strong>大一倍</strong>。正是这个选择让它变得便宜，你马上就会看到。`,"Why double":`为什么翻倍`,"One extra cell would mean moving everything again on the very next append.":`只多一格的话，下一次追加就又得把所有东西搬一遍。`,"Move everything across":`全部搬过去`,"Every item is moved into the new array, one at a time, keeping its index.":`每一项都被搬进新数组，一次一个，下标保持不变。`,"This is the expensive part: three items, three moves. With a million items it would be a million.":`这是昂贵的部分：三个项，三次移动。如果有一百万个项，就是一百万次。`,"A grow is O(n). It is the price of the append that triggered it.":`一次扩容是 O(n)。这是触发它的那次追加付出的代价。`,"Swap, then append":`替换，然后追加`,"The old array is let go and the new one takes its place. To the rest of the program it is the same list: same items, same indexes.":`旧数组被释放，新数组取代它的位置。对程序的其他部分来说，它还是同一个列表：同样的项，同样的下标。`,"And now there is a cell 3. 21 goes in.":`现在有格子 3 了。21 放进去。`,"Cheap again":`又便宜了`,"34 and 55 go straight in: the doubling bought three free cells. Then it is full again, and the next grow will make 12.":`34 和 55 直接放进去：翻倍换来了三个空格子。然后又满了，下一次扩容会得到 12 格。`,"Each grow is twice as far away as the last. Spread over all the appends, the moving comes to about one extra step each: appending is O(1) <strong>on average</strong>. Averaging a cost over a whole run of operations like this is called <strong>amortized</strong> analysis.":`每次扩容都比上一次隔得远一倍。把搬运分摊到所有追加上，每次大约只多一步：追加<strong>平均</strong>是 O(1)。像这样把代价平摊到一整串操作上，叫作<strong>均摊</strong>分析。`,"This is the list in Python, the ArrayList in Java, the vector in C++.":`这就是 Python 的 list、Java 的 ArrayList、C++ 的 vector。`,"Six appends, three moves.":`六次追加，三次移动。`},"two-pointers":{"left ← 0, right ← last index":`left ← 0，right ← 最后一个下标`,"while left < right:":`当 left < right:`,"if sum = target: return left, right":`如果 sum = target: 返回 left, right`,"if sum < target: left ← left + 1":`如果 sum < target: left ← left + 1`,"else: right ← right − 1":`否则: right ← right − 1`,"How many looks":`看了几次`,"A sorted row":`排好序的一排`,"Seven numbers, in order. Which two of them add up to <strong>14</strong>?":`七个数，按顺序排列。哪两个加起来等于 <strong>14</strong>？`,"You could try every pair, but there are 21 of them. Because the row is sorted, two markers can do it in a handful of looks.":`你可以试遍每一对，但一共有 21 对。因为这一排是排好序的，两个标记看几次就能解决。`,"Like binary search, this only works on sorted data.":`和二分查找一样，这只适用于排好序的数据。`,"Looks so far":`已看次数`,"Pairs there are":`总对数`,"Trying every pair is O(n²).":`试遍每一对是 O(n²)。`,"Start at both ends":`从两端开始`,"Put <strong>left</strong> on the smallest value and <strong>right</strong> on the largest, and add them.":`把 <strong>left</strong> 放在最小的值上，<strong>right</strong> 放在最大的值上，把它们加起来。`,"1 + 15 = 16. That is more than 14.":`1 + 15 = 16。比 14 大。`,"15 is too big to pair with anything: even with the smallest value it overshoots.":`15 太大，和谁配对都不行：即使配上最小的值也超了。`,"1 + 15 = 16 · too big":`1 + 15 = 16 · 太大`,"Too big: step right in":`太大：right 往里走`,"So 15 is out for good. Move <strong>right</strong> one place in, and add again.":`所以 15 永远出局了。把 <strong>right</strong> 往里移一格，再加一次。`,"1 + 12 = 13. Now it is less than 14.":`1 + 12 = 13。现在比 14 小。`,"1 is too small to pair with anything that is left.":`1 太小，和剩下的任何值配对都不够。`,"1 + 12 = 13 · too small":`1 + 12 = 13 · 太小`,"Too small: step left in":`太小：left 往里走`,"1 is out. Move <strong>left</strong> one place in.":`1 出局。把 <strong>left</strong> 往里移一格。`,"4 + 12 = 16. Too big again, so it is right’s turn to move.":`4 + 12 = 16。又太大了，所以轮到 right 移动。`,"4 + 12 = 16 · too big":`4 + 12 = 16 · 太大`,"12 is out, and <strong>right</strong> steps in to 10.":`12 出局，<strong>right</strong> 往里走到 10。`,"4 + 10 = 14. That is the pair, at indexes 1 and 4.":`4 + 10 = 14。就是这一对，下标是 1 和 4。`,"Had the two markers met without a match, there would be no such pair.":`如果两个标记相遇时还没找到，那就不存在这样的一对。`,"Four looks, instead of up to 21.":`看了四次，而不是最多 21 次。`,"Every look ruled one value out for good, and a marker never moves back.":`每看一次就永久排除一个值，而且标记从不后退。`,"So there can be at most n looks before the markers meet: <strong>O(n)</strong>, against O(n²) for trying every pair.":`所以在两个标记相遇之前，最多看 n 次：<strong>O(n)</strong>，而试遍每一对是 O(n²)。`,"The same two-ended squeeze reverses a list in place and checks for a palindrome.":`同样的两端夹逼法，也能原地反转列表、检查回文。`},"sliding-window":{"sum ← total of the first k items":`sum ← 前 k 项的总和`,"for each step to the right:":`对每个 向右的一步:`,"sum ← sum − the item leaving":`sum ← sum − 离开的项`,"sum ← sum + the item entering":`sum ← sum + 进入的项`,"if sum > best: best ← sum":`如果 sum > best: best ← sum`,"Window sums":`窗口的和`,"Best run of three":`最好的连续三个`,"Seven numbers in a row. Which three <em>next to each other</em> add up to the most?":`一排七个数。哪三个<em>相邻</em>的数加起来最大？`,"You could add up every run of three from scratch. But each run shares two of its numbers with the one before, so most of that adding is repeated.":`你可以把每组连续三个都从头加一遍。但每组都和前一组共用两个数，所以大部分加法都是重复的。`,"A window three cells wide, sliding along the row.":`一个三格宽的窗口，沿着这一排滑动。`,"Sums so far":`已算的和`,Best:`最好`,"The first window":`第一个窗口`,Start:`开始`,"Put the window over the first three values and add them up, the ordinary way.":`把窗口放在前三个值上，用普通的方法加起来。`,"4 + 2 + 7 = 13. That is the best so far, because it is the only one so far.":`4 + 2 + 7 = 13。这是目前最好的，因为目前只有它一个。`,"Slide, don’t start over":`滑动，不要重来`,"Move the window one cell right. One value leaves on the left and one enters on the right; the two in the middle were already counted.":`把窗口右移一格。左边离开一个值，右边进来一个值；中间两个已经算过了。`,"So take the old sum, subtract what left and add what came in: 13 − 4 + 1 = 10.":`所以拿旧的和，减去离开的，加上进来的：13 − 4 + 1 = 10。`,"Two operations, however wide the window is.":`两次运算，不管窗口有多宽。`,"Keep the best":`保留最好的`,"Slide again: 10 − 2 + 8 = 16.":`再滑一次：10 − 2 + 8 = 16。`,"That beats 13, so it becomes the best so far.":`比 13 大，所以它成为目前最好的。`,"To the end":`一直到底`,"Two more slides reach the end of the row: 12, then 17.":`再滑两次就到这一排的末尾：12，然后是 17。`,"The best run of three is 8, 3, 6.":`最好的连续三个是 8、3、6。`,"Each value entered the window once and left it once. That is all the work there was: <strong>O(n)</strong>.":`每个值进窗口一次、出窗口一次。全部工作就这么多：<strong>O(n)</strong>。`,"Adding every run from scratch would be O(n × k), and it gets worse the wider the window.":`每组都从头加是 O(n × k)，窗口越宽越糟。`,"The same idea finds the longest stretch of text without a repeated letter. There the window grows and shrinks.":`同样的思路可以找出最长的没有重复字母的一段文字。那时窗口会变大也会变小。`,"Seven values, five windows, four slides.":`七个值，五个窗口，滑动四次。`},"prefix-sums":{"for each i from 1 to the last:":`对于 i 从 1 到最后一个:`,"if i = 0: return total[j]":`如果 i = 0: 返回 total[j]`,"return total[j] − total[i − 1]":`返回 total[j] − total[i − 1]`,"Check it":`验证一下`,"Adding up a stretch":`把一段加起来`,"What do cells 1 to 4 add up to? Add them one at a time: 1 + 4 + 1 + 5 = 11.":`格子 1 到 4 加起来是多少？一个一个加：1 + 4 + 1 + 5 = 11。`,"That is fine once. But asked about a hundred different stretches, you would add the same numbers again and again.":`一次还好。但如果要问一百个不同的区段，你就会一遍又一遍地加同样的数。`,"O(n) for every question: the longer the stretch, the more to add.":`每个问题都是 O(n)：区段越长，要加的越多。`,"Adding them up":`逐个相加`,"With the totals":`用累计和`,"Do the adding once, up front. Walk along the row keeping a <strong>running total</strong>, and write it down behind each value.":`先把加法一次做完。沿着这一排走，维护一个<strong>累计和</strong>，并把它写在每个值的后面。`,"Each total is the one before it plus the value in front of it: 3, then 3 + 1 = 4, then 4 + 4 = 8, and so on.":`每个累计和都等于前一个累计和加上它前面的值：3，然后 3 + 1 = 4，然后 4 + 4 = 8，依此类推。`,"“Everything from the start up to here.”":`“从开头到这里的全部。”`,"Six additions, done once.":`六次加法，只做一次。`,"One subtraction":`一次减法`,"Now ask again: cells 1 to 4. Everything up to cell 4 is 14. Everything <em>before</em> cell 1 is 3.":`现在再问：格子 1 到 4。到格子 4 为止的全部是 14。格子 1 <em>之前</em>的全部是 3。`,"Take one from the other and what is left is exactly the stretch: 14 − 3 = 11.":`一个减去另一个，剩下的正好就是这一段：14 − 3 = 11。`,"The values themselves were not touched. Two totals did it.":`值本身完全没动。两个累计和就解决了。`,"Any stretch":`任意一段`,"Cells 3 to 5: the total up to cell 5 is 23, and before cell 3 it is 8.":`格子 3 到 5：到格子 5 的累计和是 23，格子 3 之前是 8。`,"23 − 8 = 15, however long the stretch is.":`23 − 8 = 15，不管这一段有多长。`,"O(1) for every question.":`每个问题都是 O(1)。`,"From the start":`从开头开始`,"Cells 0 to 3 start at the very beginning, so there is nothing before them to take away.":`格子 0 到 3 从最开头开始，所以前面没有什么要减的。`,"The answer is just the total up to cell 3: 9.":`答案就是到格子 3 的累计和：9。`,"Without this case you would look for a total before the first one.":`没有这个情况，你就会去找第一个累计和之前的累计和。`,"One pass to build the totals, then every question is a single subtraction.":`一趟构建累计和，之后每个问题都只是一次减法。`,"It costs a second row of memory. And if a value changes, every total after it is wrong and has to be rebuilt.":`代价是多一排内存。而且如果某个值变了，它后面的每个累计和都错了，必须重建。`,"Many questions about data that stays put: prefix sums. Data that keeps changing: something else.":`对不变的数据问很多问题：用前缀和。数据一直在变：用别的方法。`,"Build: O(n), once. Ask: O(1), every time.":`构建：O(n)，一次。查询：O(1)，每次。`},"maximum-subarray":{"best ← the first item":`best ← 第一项`,"if run > best: best ← run":`如果 run > best: best ← run`,"if run < 0: run ← 0     // a run in debt is dropped":`如果 run < 0: run ← 0     // 欠债的累计直接丢掉`,Totals:`累计`,"The best stretch":`最好的一段`,"Some of these numbers are gains and some are losses. Which unbroken stretch adds up to the most?":`这些数有的是收益，有的是亏损。哪一段连续的数加起来最大？`,"There are n² stretches to try. But one pass along the row is enough, if you carry the right two numbers with you.":`要试的区段有 n² 个。但只要随身带着对的两个数，沿着这一排走一趟就够了。`,"Current run":`当前累计`,"Best so far":`目前最好`,"Walk along the row adding each number to a <strong>run</strong>. After the first cell the run is 3, and that is also the best seen so far.":`沿着这一排走，把每个数加到一个<strong>累计</strong>上。过了第一个格子，累计是 3，这也是目前见过最好的。`,"Drop a run in debt":`丢掉欠债的累计`,"Adding −4 takes the run to −1. A run that has gone negative can only drag down whatever comes next.":`加上 −4，累计变成 −1。一个已经变成负数的累计，只会拖累后面的任何东西。`,"So forget it. The next cell starts a new run from nothing. The best so far is still 3.":`所以忘掉它。下一个格子从零开始新的累计。目前最好的仍然是 3。`,"The whole trick":`全部的诀窍`,"Anything that sums to less than zero is not worth carrying forward.":`任何加起来小于零的东西，都不值得带着往前走。`,"run = −1: drop it":`run = −1：丢掉`,"Start afresh":`重新开始`,"5 begins a new run, and 5 beats the old best of 3.":`5 开始了新的累计，而 5 超过了旧的最好值 3。`,"A dip can be worth it":`下跌也可能值得`,"−2 lowers the run to 3. That is still positive, so it is kept. Then 4 lifts it to 7: a new best.":`−2 把累计降到 3。仍然是正数，所以保留。然后 4 把它抬到 7：新的最好值。`,"A small loss was worth sitting through for what came after it.":`为了后面的收获，熬过一个小亏损是值得的。`,"−6 and 1 leave the run at 2, which never beats 7. The best stretch is 5, −2, 4.":`−6 和 1 让累计停在 2，永远超不过 7。最好的一段是 5、−2、4。`,"Every number was looked at once. This is Kadane’s algorithm, and it is dynamic programming in its smallest form: the best run ending here depends only on the best run ending one cell back.":`每个数都只看了一次。这就是 Kadane 算法，它是最小形式的动态规划：以这里结尾的最好累计，只取决于以前一格结尾的最好累计。`,"O(n) time and two variables of memory.":`O(n) 时间，内存只要两个变量。`,here:`这里`},"merge-intervals":{"sort them by where they start":`按起点排序`,"run ← the first interval":`run ← 第一个区间`,"for each of the others:":`对每个 其余的区间:`,"if it starts before run ends:":`如果 它在 run 结束之前开始:`,"stretch run to cover it":`拉长 run 来覆盖它`,"keep run, and start a new one here":`保留 run，并在这里开始新的一段`,"keep the last run":`保留最后一段`,"On the timeline":`在时间轴上`,"Overlapping stretches":`重叠的区段`,"Three bookings on a timeline. Each row is one booking; the blocks are the hours it covers. Some overlap.":`时间轴上有三个预订。每一行是一个预订；方块是它占用的小时。有些重叠了。`,"Combine any that overlap, so that what is left is a list of separate busy stretches. Calendars, memory allocators and genome tools all need this.":`把重叠的合并起来，剩下的就是一张互不相交的忙碌时段列表。日历、内存分配器和基因组工具都需要这个。`,Intervals:`区间`,Merged:`合并后`,"Sort by start":`按起点排序`,"Put the intervals in order of where they begin. These already are: 0, 1, 6.":`把区间按开始的位置排好。这些已经排好了：0、1、6。`,"Sorted this way, anything that overlaps an interval must come straight after it. One pass will be enough.":`这样排序后，任何与某个区间重叠的区间，一定紧跟在它后面。一趟就够了。`,"Start a run":`开始一段`,"Begin the result with the first interval: a run from 0 to 2.":`用第一个区间开始结果：一段从 0 到 2。`,"It overlaps: stretch":`重叠了：拉长`,"B starts at 1. The run does not end until 2, so they overlap. Stretch the run to wherever B ends: 4.":`B 从 1 开始。这一段要到 2 才结束，所以它们重叠。把这一段拉长到 B 结束的地方：4。`,"Only two numbers were compared: B’s start and the run’s end.":`只比较了两个数：B 的起点和这一段的终点。`,"starts inside the run":`在这一段内部开始`,"A gap: start again":`有空隙：重新开始`,"C starts at 6, after the run has ended at 4. There is a gap, so the run is finished. Keep it, and start a new one at C.":`C 从 6 开始，这时这一段已经在 4 结束了。有空隙，所以这一段完成了。保留它，从 C 开始新的一段。`,"starts after it ended":`在它结束之后开始`,"Two stretches":`两个区段`,"Three bookings became two busy stretches. Each interval was looked at once, after sorting.":`三个预订变成了两个忙碌时段。排序之后，每个区间只看了一次。`,"Sorting first is what makes it easy. Without it, every interval would have to be checked against every other.":`先排序才让它变得容易。不排序的话，每个区间都得和其他每个区间比一遍。`,"O(n log n) for the sort, then O(n) for the pass.":`排序 O(n log n)，然后一趟 O(n)。`},"pattern-matching":{"for each place the pattern could start:":`对每个 模式可能开始的位置:`,"compare it with the text, letter by letter":`把它和文本逐个字母比较`,"if every letter matches: return this place":`如果 每个字母都匹配: 返回 这个位置`,"Find one string in another":`在一个字符串里找另一个`,"A string is an array of characters. The commonest thing to ask of one is whether it contains another: is ABAC somewhere in ABABAC?":`字符串是字符的数组。对字符串最常问的，就是它是否包含另一个字符串：ABAC 在 ABABAC 里吗？`,"The text is the row behind. The pattern starts lined up with its beginning.":`文本是后面那一排。模式一开始和它的开头对齐。`,"Letter by letter":`逐个字母`,"Compare the pattern with the text beneath it, left to right. A and A, B and B, A and A: three matches.":`从左到右，把模式和它下面的文本比较。A 和 A，B 和 B，A 和 A：三个匹配。`,"A mismatch":`不匹配`,"The fourth letter fails: the pattern wants C, and the text has B. The pattern is not here.":`第四个字母失败了：模式要 C，文本是 B。模式不在这里。`,"Slide along and start again":`往后滑，重新开始`,"The simple method moves the pattern one place to the right and begins again from its first letter. This time it fails at once: A against B.":`简单的方法把模式右移一位，再从它的第一个字母开始。这次马上就失败了：A 对 B。`,"A match":`匹配`,"One more place along, and all four letters agree. The pattern is in the text, starting at index 2.":`再往后一位，四个字母全都一致。模式在文本里，从下标 2 开始。`,"Do not look twice":`别看两遍`,Faster:`更快`,"Nine comparisons, and some were wasted. When the first try failed, three letters had already matched, so the text there was known to be A B A. Starting at the next place could never have worked.":`九次比较，有些是浪费的。第一次尝试失败时，已经有三个字母匹配了，所以已知那里的文本是 A B A。从下一个位置开始根本不可能成功。`,"Smarter methods use what has already matched to jump straight to the next place that could. The best known, KMP, never moves backwards in the text.":`更聪明的方法利用已经匹配的部分，直接跳到下一个可能成功的位置。最有名的 KMP，在文本里从不回头。`,"Slide-and-retry is O(n × m) at worst. KMP is O(n + m).":`逐位滑动重试最坏是 O(n × m)。KMP 是 O(n + m)。`,"a jump of 2 would do":`跳 2 格就行`,"With the jump: 8 comparisons.":`跳着走：8 次比较。`},kmp:r,matrices:i,"linked-lists":{"next → the node after it, or nothing":`next → 它后面的节点，或者空`,"repeat k times:":`重复 k 次:`,"return cur":`返回 cur`,"node ← a new node holding value":`node ← 一个存放 value 的新节点`,"A chain of nodes":`一串节点`,"A linked list keeps each value in its own <strong>node</strong>. Next to the value, the node stores a pointer to the node that comes after it.":`链表把每个值放在它自己的<strong>节点</strong>里。在值的旁边，节点存着一个指向下一个节点的指针。`,"The list itself only remembers where the first node is: the <strong>head</strong>. The last node points at nothing.":`链表本身只记得第一个节点在哪里：也就是<strong>头节点</strong>。最后一个节点什么都不指向。`,"The beads show the order the list is read in: from the head, along one pointer after another.":`珠子表示读取链表的顺序：从头节点开始，沿着一个又一个指针走。`,"A treasure hunt. Each clue tells you where to find the next one.":`寻宝游戏。每条线索都告诉你下一条在哪里。`,"Follow the pointers":`沿着指针走`,Traversal:`遍历`,"Nodes have no index numbers. To reach the third one you start at the head and hop along the pointers, one node at a time.":`节点没有下标。要到达第三个节点，你得从头节点出发，沿着指针一次跳一个节点。`,"Look at the table: the nodes are not even next to each other in memory. Only the pointers put them in order.":`看看这张表：这些节点在内存中甚至不是挨着的。只有指针让它们有了顺序。`,"Reaching item k takes k hops: O(n). An array jumps straight there.":`到达第 k 项需要跳 k 次：O(n)。数组可以直接跳过去。`,"A new node":`一个新节点`,"Insert · 1 of 3":`插入 · 第 1 步，共 3 步`,"Let’s add <strong>33</strong> after 27. First make a node for it.":`我们在 27 后面加入 <strong>33</strong>。先为它造一个节点。`,"It can live anywhere in memory. Nothing points at it yet, so it is not part of the list: it hangs off to one side, and the beads go straight past.":`它可以放在内存的任何地方。还没有东西指向它，所以它还不是链表的一部分：它悬在一边，珠子直接从旁边经过。`,"Nobody had to make room for it. The other nodes stay exactly where they are.":`没有谁需要为它腾地方。其他节点都待在原地不动。`,"Point it forward":`让它指向前方`,"Insert · 2 of 3":`插入 · 第 2 步，共 3 步`,"Copy 27’s pointer into the new node, so that 33 points at 45.":`把 27 的指针复制到新节点里，这样 33 就指向 45。`,"The list still runs 12 → 27 → 45. Nothing is broken, and nothing can see 33 yet.":`链表仍然是 12 → 27 → 45。什么都没坏，也还没有谁能看到 33。`,"Order matters":`顺序很重要`,"Do this first. Re-point 27 first and you lose the only way to reach 45.":`先做这一步。如果先改 27 的指针，你就失去了到达 45 的唯一途径。`,"Re-link":`重新连接`,"Insert · 3 of 3":`插入 · 第 3 步，共 3 步`,"Now point 27 at the new node. 33 is part of the list, so it takes its place in line: 12 → 27 → 33 → 45.":`现在让 27 指向新节点。33 成了链表的一部分，于是在队列中就位：12 → 27 → 33 → 45。`,"The drawing makes room for it, but look at the table: no node changed address. Two pointer writes did it all. An array would have had to move 45 in memory.":`图上为它腾出了位置，但看看这张表：没有一个节点改变地址。两次指针写入就完成了一切。数组的话就得在内存中移动 45。`,"O(1) once you are standing at the spot.":`只要你已经站在那个位置，就是 O(1)。`,"Delete by bypass":`绕过即删除`,Delete:`删除`,"To remove 27, point the node before it straight past it: 12 now points at 33.":`要删除 27，就让它前面的节点直接越过它：12 现在指向 33。`,"27 still points at 33, but nothing points at 27. It drops out of the line, and the list closes up without it.":`27 仍然指向 33，但没有东西指向 27 了。它掉出了队列，链表在没有它的情况下重新接上。`,"One pointer write: O(1), again once you are at the spot.":`一次指针写入：O(1)，同样前提是你已经在那个位置。`,"The unreachable node drifts off to be cleaned up, and the list is 12 → 33 → 45.":`无法到达的节点飘走，等着被清理，链表变成 12 → 33 → 45。`,"Linked lists make adding and removing cheap. They pay for it with slow lookups and one extra pointer per item.":`链表让添加和删除变得便宜。代价是查找慢，以及每项多一个指针。`,"Lots of inserting and removing in the middle: linked list. Lots of “give me item k”: array.":`经常在中间插入和删除：用链表。经常“给我第 k 项”：用数组。`},"doubly-linked-lists":{"visit cur":`访问 cur`,"make a node n holding x":`新建一个存放 x 的节点 n`,"Singly or doubly":`单向还是双向`,"A pointer each way":`每个方向一个指针`,"A singly linked node knows only what comes after it. A <strong>doubly linked</strong> node keeps a second pointer, <em>prev</em>, to the node before.":`单向链表的节点只知道它后面是什么。<strong>双向链表</strong>的节点还存着第二个指针 <em>prev</em>，指向前一个节点。`,"The list also remembers both ends: <em>head</em> and <em>tail</em>. Now it can be read in either direction.":`链表也记住两端：<em>head</em> 和 <em>tail</em>。现在两个方向都能读了。`,"A train where every carriage is coupled to the one in front and the one behind.":`一列火车，每节车厢都和前一节、后一节挂在一起。`,"Walk backwards":`反向遍历`,cannot:`不能`,can:`能`,"Remove a node you hold":`删除手上的节点`,"Add or remove at the tail":`在尾部添加或删除`,"Pointers in every node":`每个节点的指针数`,"Left: singly linked. Right: doubly linked.":`左：单向链表。右：双向链表。`,"Walk it backwards":`反向遍历`,"Start at the tail and follow the prev pointers: 27, then 20, then 12.":`从 tail 开始，沿着 prev 指针走：27，然后 20，然后 12。`,"A singly linked list cannot do this at all. Its pointers only lead one way.":`单向链表完全做不到这一点。它的指针只通向一个方向。`,"Holding a node":`手上拿着一个节点`,"Suppose you already have hold of 20, and want it out of the list.":`假设你已经拿到了 20，想把它从链表里拿掉。`,"With one pointer per node you would be stuck: removing it means changing the node <em>before</em> it, and the only way to find that is to walk from the head.":`如果每个节点只有一个指针，你就卡住了：删除它意味着要修改它<em>前面</em>的节点，而找到那个节点的唯一方法是从头节点走过去。`,"Unhook it both sides":`从两边解开它`,"Here 20 knows both its neighbours. Tell the one before to skip ahead, and the one after to skip back: two pointers rewritten, no walking.":`这里 20 知道它的两个邻居。告诉前一个节点往前跳过它，告诉后一个节点往回跳过它：改写两个指针，不用遍历。`,"Nothing points at 20 any more, so it is out of the list, and the list closes up.":`不再有东西指向 20，所以它离开了链表，链表重新接上。`,"O(1), wherever the node is. At either end, head or tail moves instead.":`O(1)，不管节点在哪里。在两端的话，改为移动 head 或 tail。`,"Add at the tail":`在尾部添加`,"The tail pointer makes the far end as easy to reach as the near one. To add 33, hook it to the old tail both ways and move tail along.":`有了 tail 指针，远端和近端一样容易到达。要添加 33，就把它和旧的尾节点双向连起来，再把 tail 移过去。`,"Removing the last node is just as quick, because the tail knows what is before it.":`删除最后一个节点也一样快，因为尾节点知道它前面是谁。`,"None of this is free. Every node carries a second pointer, and every change has more pointers to keep right: miss one and the list reads differently forwards and backwards.":`这些都不是免费的。每个节点都多带一个指针，每次修改都有更多指针要保持正确：漏掉一个，链表正着读和反着读就不一样了。`,"Use one when you need to move both ways or remove from the middle: browser history, undo and redo, caches that drop the oldest entry.":`需要双向移动或从中间删除时就用它：浏览器历史、撤销和重做、丢弃最旧条目的缓存。`,"Singly linked when you only ever go forwards. Doubly linked when you do not.":`只往前走就用单向链表。不是的话就用双向链表。`},"fast-slow":{"while fast can make two more hops:":`当 fast 还能再跳两次:`,"return slow":`返回 slow`,"if slow = fast: return yes":`如果 slow = fast: 返回 是`,"return no                // fast ran off the end":`返回 否                // fast 跑到了尽头`,"The two cursors":`两个游标`,"Two cursors, two speeds":`两个游标，两种速度`,"A linked list has no indexes and does not know its own length. To find its middle you could walk it once to count, then again to the halfway point.":`链表没有下标，也不知道自己的长度。要找到中间，你可以先走一遍数个数，再走到一半的位置。`,"Or send <strong>two cursors</strong> down it together: <em>slow</em> takes one hop at a time, <em>fast</em> takes two.":`或者让<strong>两个游标</strong>一起走：<em>slow</em> 一次跳一步，<em>fast</em> 一次跳两步。`,"Also known as":`又称`,"The tortoise and the hare.":`龟兔赛跑。`,"slow is on":`slow 在`,"0 hops":`跳 0 次`,"fast is on":`fast 在`,"Both start at the head.":`两个都从头节点开始。`,"One round":`一轮`,"In each round slow follows one pointer and fast follows two.":`每一轮 slow 沿一个指针走，fast 沿两个指针走。`,"After one round slow is on 8 and fast is on 12. Fast is always twice as far from the head as slow.":`一轮之后 slow 在 8，fast 在 12。fast 离头节点的距离总是 slow 的两倍。`,"1 hop":`跳 1 次`,"2 hops":`跳 2 次`,"The middle":`中间`,"Another round, and fast is on the last node: it cannot make two more hops, so the walk stops.":`再走一轮，fast 到了最后一个节点：它不能再跳两次了，所以停下。`,"Fast has covered the whole list. Slow has covered half of it, so slow is standing on the <strong>middle</strong>.":`fast 走完了整个链表。slow 走了一半，所以 slow 正站在<strong>中间</strong>。`,"One pass, no counting, and only two cursors of extra memory.":`一趟，不用计数，额外的内存只有两个游标。`,"4 hops":`跳 4 次`,"Fast went twice as far.":`fast 走了两倍远。`,"A list with a loop":`带环的链表`,"Now a bug: the last node points back into the list instead of at nothing. There is no end any more.":`现在出了个 bug：最后一个节点不是指向空，而是指回链表里。再也没有尽头了。`,"Anything that walks this list “until null” will go round for ever. How can a program tell, without remembering every node it has seen?":`任何“一直走到 null”的遍历都会永远绕圈。程序怎样才能发现这一点，而不用记住见过的每个节点？`,"Back at the head, ready to try.":`回到头节点，准备尝试。`,"Send them round":`让它们绕圈`,"Use the same two cursors. After two rounds slow is on 12 and fast is on 27, just as before.":`用同样的两个游标。两轮之后 slow 在 12，fast 在 27，和之前一样。`,"Last time the walk ended here. This time fast still has somewhere to go.":`上次遍历在这里就结束了。这次 fast 还有地方可去。`,"Fast comes up behind":`fast 从后面追上来`,"Fast follows the pointer round the back and lands on 12, where slow has just left: slow is one node ahead, on 20.":`fast 沿着指针绕到后面，落在 12 上，而 slow 刚刚离开那里：slow 领先一个节点，在 20 上。`,"Inside a loop there is no “ahead” for long. Each round fast gains one node on slow.":`在环里，“领先”维持不了多久。每一轮 fast 都比 slow 多追上一个节点。`,"3 hops":`跳 3 次`,"6 hops":`跳 6 次`,"Fast is one node behind slow.":`fast 落后 slow 一个节点。`,"They meet":`它们相遇了`,"One more round and they are on the same node. Two cursors moving forward at different speeds can only meet if the list bends back on itself: <strong>there is a loop</strong>.":`再走一轮，它们就在同一个节点上了。两个以不同速度前进的游标，只有在链表绕回自身时才会相遇：<strong>有环</strong>。`,"If there were none, fast would simply have reached the end, as it did before.":`如果没有环，fast 就会像之前那样直接走到尽头。`,"O(n) time and no extra memory. Remembering every visited node would cost O(n) memory.":`O(n) 时间，不用额外内存。记住每个访问过的节点要花 O(n) 内存。`,"they meet: a loop":`相遇了：有环`,"8 hops":`跳 8 次`,"Same node: the list has a loop.":`同一个节点：链表有环。`},"reversing-a-list":{"prev ← nothing":`prev ← 空`,"next ← cur.next      // remember the rest":`next ← cur.next      // 记住剩下的部分`,"cur.next ← prev      // turn the pointer round":`cur.next ← prev      // 把指针掉头`,"prev ← cur           // step along":`prev ← cur           // 往前走一步`,"return prev              // the new head":`返回 prev              // 新的头节点`,"Two halves":`两半`,"Turn every pointer round":`把每个指针都掉头`,"This list reads 12, 20, 27, 33. Reverse it, so it reads 33, 27, 20, 12.":`这个链表读作 12、20、27、33。把它反转，让它读作 33、27、20、12。`,"With an array you would swap values. With a linked list the nodes can stay exactly where they are: only the <strong>pointers</strong> need to turn round.":`用数组的话你会交换值。用链表的话，节点可以原地不动：只有<strong>指针</strong>需要掉头。`,"Turned round":`已掉头`,"Still to do":`还没处理`,"Three cursors":`三个游标`,"Turning 12’s pointer round would cut off the rest of the list, so first take hold of it: <em>next</em> remembers the node after <em>cur</em>.":`把 12 的指针掉头会切断链表剩下的部分，所以先抓住它：<em>next</em> 记住 <em>cur</em> 后面的节点。`,"<em>prev</em> is what cur should point at instead. For the first node that is nothing at all: it will be the new end.":`<em>prev</em> 是 cur 应该改为指向的东西。对第一个节点来说，那就是空：它会成为新的末尾。`,"Forget to save next and the rest of the list is unreachable the moment you rewrite the pointer.":`忘了保存 next，在你改写指针的那一刻，链表剩下的部分就再也到不了了。`,"Turn the pointer":`把指针掉头`,Rewrite:`改写`,"Now it is safe. <strong>cur.next ← prev</strong>: 12 stops pointing at 20 and points back at nothing.":`现在安全了。<strong>cur.next ← prev</strong>：12 不再指向 20，而是指回空。`,"The list is in two pieces for the moment, and the cursors are holding one end of each.":`链表暂时分成了两段，游标各抓着一段的一头。`,"Step along":`往前走一步`,Advance:`前进`,"All three cursors move one node on: prev takes cur’s place, cur takes next’s, and next looks one further.":`三个游标都往前移一个节点：prev 占据 cur 的位置，cur 占据 next 的位置，next 再往前看一个。`,"Everything behind cur is already reversed. Everything from cur onwards is untouched.":`cur 后面的部分都已经反转了。从 cur 往后的部分还没动过。`,"The same two moves. 20’s pointer swings back to 12, then the cursors step along.":`同样的两个动作。20 的指针转回指向 12，然后游标往前走。`,"One node joins the reversed part each time.":`每次都有一个节点加入已反转的部分。`,"27 now points back at 20. Looking ahead, next finds nothing after 33: one node to go.":`27 现在指回 20。往前看，next 发现 33 后面什么都没有：还剩一个节点。`,"Off the end":`走出尽头`,"33 turns to point at 27, and cur steps off the end of the list. There is nothing left to turn round, so the loop stops.":`33 转为指向 27，cur 走出了链表的尽头。没有需要掉头的了，循环停止。`,"prev is standing on 33: the last node that was handled.":`prev 站在 33 上：最后处理的那个节点。`,"A new head":`新的头节点`,"One thing is still wrong: head points at 12, which is now the end. Move it to where prev is.":`还有一处不对：head 指向 12，而它现在是末尾。把它移到 prev 所在的地方。`,"The list reads 33, 27, 20, 12. No node moved and none was copied: one pass, and three cursors of extra memory.":`链表读作 33、27、20、12。没有节点移动，也没有节点被复制：一趟，额外内存只有三个游标。`,"O(n) time, O(1) extra space.":`O(n) 时间，O(1) 额外空间。`,"Reversed in place.":`原地反转完成。`},"merge-sorted-lists":{"tail ← a dummy node before the result":`tail ← 结果前面的一个哑节点`,"while both lists have nodes:":`当 两个链表都还有节点:`,"take whichever front node is smaller":`取两个队首节点中较小的那个`,"tail.next ← that node":`tail.next ← 那个节点`,"tail ← that node":`tail ← 那个节点`,"tail.next ← whatever list is left":`tail.next ← 剩下的那个链表`,"return the node after the dummy":`返回 哑节点后面的节点`,"The merge":`合并`,"Two lists into one":`两个链表合成一个`,"Two linked lists, each already in order: 1, 4, 6 in front and 2, 3, 5 behind. Combine them into one sorted list.":`两个链表，各自已经有序：前面是 1、4、6，后面是 2、3、5。把它们合并成一个有序链表。`,"With arrays this needs a third array to copy into. With linked lists, no node is copied or moved in memory. Only pointers change.":`用数组的话，需要第三个数组来复制。用链表的话，没有节点在内存中被复制或移动。只有指针会变。`,"Merged so far":`已合并`,"Front of list A":`链表 A 的队首`,"Front of list B":`链表 B 的队首`,"Compare the fronts":`比较队首`,"Both lists are sorted, so the smallest node overall is at the front of one of them. 1 is smaller than 2: it becomes the head of the result.":`两个链表都是有序的，所以全部节点中最小的一定在其中一个的队首。1 比 2 小：它成为结果的头节点。`,"Splice the smaller one in":`把较小的接进来`,"Now the fronts are 4 and 2. 2 is smaller, so it comes next: point 1 at 2, and 2 on to whatever follows.":`现在队首是 4 和 2。2 更小，所以它是下一个：让 1 指向 2，2 再指向后面跟着的东西。`,"Two pointers were rewritten. The node itself is the same node it always was.":`改写了两个指针。节点本身还是原来那个节点。`,"4 against 3: 3 is next. It goes in after 2.":`4 对 3：3 是下一个。它接在 2 后面。`,"Whichever is smaller":`哪个小取哪个`,"4 against 5: this time the node already in line wins, and nothing needs rewiring. Then 6 against 5: 5 goes in before 6.":`4 对 5：这次胜出的节点本来就在队列里，不需要重新连线。然后 6 对 5：5 插到 6 前面。`,"One list":`一个链表`,"When one list runs out, the rest of the other is already in order and already linked: attach it and stop.":`当一个链表用完时，另一个剩下的部分已经有序、已经连好了：接上去就结束。`,"Six nodes, one pass, and not one of them was copied. This is the merge step of merge sort, done on a linked list.":`六个节点，一趟，没有一个被复制。这就是归并排序的合并步骤，只不过是在链表上做的。`,"O(n + m) time and O(1) extra space.":`O(n + m) 时间，O(1) 额外空间。`},"lru-cache":{"node ← map[key]          // straight to it":`node ← map[key]          // 直接找到它`,"unhook node, put it at the front":`解开 node，把它放到最前面`,"return node.value":`返回 node.value`,"if the cache is full:":`如果 缓存已满:`,"remove the node at the back, and its key from the map":`删除最后面的节点，并从 map 中删除它的键`,"put a new node at the front":`在最前面放一个新节点`,"map[key] ← that node":`map[key] ← 那个节点`,"The cache":`缓存`,"A cache with a limit":`有上限的缓存`,"A cache keeps recent answers to hand so they need not be worked out again. It has limited room, so when it is full something must go. A good rule: throw out whatever was used <strong>least recently</strong>.":`缓存把最近的答案放在手边，省得再算一遍。它的空间有限，所以满了的时候必须扔掉一些。一个好规则：扔掉<strong>最久没用</strong>的那个。`,"This list holds three entries in order of use. The head is the newest, the tail the one that has gone longest untouched.":`这个链表按使用顺序存着三个条目。头部是最新的，尾部是最久没碰过的。`,"In the map":`在 map 中`,"Recently used":`最近使用`,"newest first":`最新的在前`,Room:`空间`,"3 of 3":`3 / 3`,"Find it at once":`一下就找到`,Get:`获取`,"Ask for A. Walking the list to find it would be O(n). So beside the list there is a <strong>hash map</strong> from each key to its node, and the map goes straight there.":`请求 A。遍历链表去找它是 O(n)。所以链表旁边有一个<strong>哈希表</strong>，从每个键映射到它的节点，哈希表直接就能找到。`,"The map points at A’s node.":`map 指向 A 的节点。`,"Unhook it":`解开它`,"A has just been used, so it is no longer the oldest. Take it out of its place: because the list is doubly linked, that is two pointer changes, with no searching.":`A 刚刚被用过，所以它不再是最旧的了。把它从原来的位置拿出来：因为链表是双向的，只需改两个指针，不用搜索。`,"To the front":`放到最前面`,"Put it back at the head. The list is in order of use again, and B is now the one at risk.":`把它放回头部。链表又是按使用顺序排列的了，现在面临淘汰的是 B。`,"Full: evict the oldest":`满了：淘汰最旧的`,"Now store D. There is no room, so the least recently used entry goes: whatever is at the tail. That is B. Its key is removed from the map too.":`现在存入 D。没有空间了，所以最久没用的条目要走：也就是尾部的那个。那是 B。它的键也从 map 中删除。`,"2 of 3":`2 / 3`,"B has been evicted.":`B 已被淘汰。`,"Two structures, one job":`两个结构，一份工作`,"D goes in at the head. Neither structure could do this alone: the map finds an entry instantly but has no order, and the list keeps the order but cannot find anything quickly.":`D 放进头部。这两个结构单独都做不到：哈希表能立刻找到条目，但没有顺序；链表保持顺序，但什么都找不快。`,"Together, every operation is a lookup and a few pointer changes.":`合在一起，每个操作都只是一次查找加几次指针修改。`,"O(1) for get and for put, however big the cache is.":`不管缓存多大，get 和 put 都是 O(1)。`},stacks:a,"balanced-brackets":{"for each character c:":`对每个 字符 c:`,"if c opens a bracket: push it":`如果 c 是开括号: 把它压入栈`,"if c closes one:":`如果 c 是闭括号:`,"if the stack is empty: return no":`如果 栈为空: 返回 否`,"if the top does not match c: return no":`如果 栈顶与 c 不配对: 返回 否`,pop:`弹出`,"return whether the stack is empty":`返回 栈是否为空`,"Reading along":`逐个读取`,"Does every bracket close?":`每个括号都闭合了吗？`,"Is ( [ ] ) balanced? Every opener needs a closer of the same kind, and they must close in the reverse of the order they opened.":`( [ ] ) 是匹配的吗？每个开括号都需要一个同类的闭括号，而且闭合的顺序必须和打开的顺序相反。`,"“Most recent first” is exactly what a stack does. Read the text left to right; the first character is waiting.":`“最近的优先”正是栈做的事。从左到右读文本；第一个字符在等待。`,"Characters read":`已读字符`,"Openers go on the stack":`开括号进栈`,"( opens a bracket. Nothing can be checked yet, so push it and move on. It will wait there until its closer turns up.":`( 是开括号。现在还没什么可检查的，所以把它压入栈，继续往下。它会一直在那里等，直到它的闭括号出现。`,"The newest waits on top":`最新的在顶上等`,"[ opens another. Push it. The stack now holds the brackets still open, with the most recent on top.":`[ 又是一个开括号。压入栈。现在栈里存着还没闭合的括号，最近的在顶上。`,"A closer checks the top":`闭括号检查栈顶`,"] closes a bracket. The one it must close is whichever opened last: the top of the stack. That is [, the same kind. Pop it.":`] 是闭括号。它必须闭合的，是最后打开的那个：栈顶。那是 [，同一类。弹出它。`,"[ ] match":`[ ] 配对`,"Empty at the end":`最后栈为空`,") closes (, which is now on top. Pop it. The text is finished and the stack is empty: every bracket found its partner.":`) 闭合 (，它现在在栈顶。弹出它。文本读完了，栈也空了：每个括号都找到了自己的另一半。`,"One pass, one stack.":`一趟，一个栈。`,"O(n) time. The stack is never bigger than the deepest nesting.":`O(n) 时间。栈的大小不会超过最深的嵌套层数。`,"( ) match":`( ) 配对`,"Balanced.":`匹配。`,"Three ways to fail":`三种失败`,"Take ( ] instead. The closer ] looks at the top and finds (, the wrong kind: not balanced.":`换成 ( ]。闭括号 ] 看向栈顶，发现是 (，类型不对：不匹配。`,"The other two failures: a closer arrives when the stack is empty, or the text ends with something still on the stack.":`另外两种失败：闭括号到来时栈是空的，或者文本结束时栈里还有东西。`,"Compilers, code editors, and anything that reads nested text such as HTML or JSON.":`编译器、代码编辑器，以及任何读取 HTML、JSON 这类嵌套文本的东西。`,"] cannot close (":`] 不能闭合 (`,"Not balanced.":`不匹配。`},queues:o,"circular-buffer":{"if size = capacity: error":`如果 size = capacity: 错误`,"if size = 0: error":`如果 size = 0: 错误`,"return x":`返回 x`,"The buffer":`缓冲区`,"A queue in an array":`数组里的队列`,"A queue adds at one end and removes at the other. In a plain array, removing from the front means shuffling everything else down: O(n) each time.":`队列在一端添加、在另一端移除。在普通数组里，从前面移除意味着把其他所有东西往前挪：每次都是 O(n)。`,"A <strong>circular buffer</strong> never shuffles. It keeps two indexes instead: <em>head</em>, where the next item leaves, and <em>tail</em>, where the next one goes in.":`<strong>环形缓冲区</strong>从不挪动。它改为记住两个下标：<em>head</em>，下一个项从这里离开；<em>tail</em>，下一个项从这里进入。`,"In the queue":`在队列中`,"Enqueue: write at tail":`入队：写在 tail`,"Each new item is written at tail, and tail moves one cell along. Four items in: tail is at 4.":`每个新项都写在 tail 处，然后 tail 往前移一格。进了四个项：tail 在 4。`,"Dequeue: read at head":`出队：从 head 读`,"To remove, read the item at head and move head along. A and B leave. Nothing else moved: the queue just starts further in now.":`要移除，就读出 head 处的项，并把 head 往前移。A 和 B 离开了。其他什么都没动：队列只是从更靠里的地方开始了。`,"Cells 0 and 1 are free again.":`格子 0 和 1 又空出来了。`,"Off the end, back to the start":`走出末尾，回到开头`,Wrap:`回绕`,"Two more go in, at cells 4 and 5. Tail would now be 6, but there is no cell 6. It <strong>wraps round</strong> to 0.":`又进了两个，在格子 4 和 5。tail 现在应该是 6，但没有格子 6。它<strong>回绕</strong>到 0。`,"That is the “mod capacity” in the code, and it is the whole idea: the end of the array is joined to its beginning.":`这就是代码里的“mod capacity”，也是整个思路所在：数组的末尾和开头连在一起。`,"Reusing the space":`重复利用空间`,"G goes into cell 0, the space A left behind. In the array it looks out of order. Read from head, wrapping at the end, it is exactly right: C, D, E, F, G.":`G 放进格子 0，也就是 A 留下的空位。在数组里它看起来顺序是乱的。从 head 开始读，到末尾就回绕，顺序完全正确：C、D、E、F、G。`,"Round and round":`一圈又一圈`,"C and D leave, and head moves on to 4. The live part of the queue now runs off the end of the array and back in at the start.":`C 和 D 离开，head 移到 4。队列中有效的部分现在跨过数组的末尾，又从开头接回来。`,"Nothing was ever shifted, and no memory was asked for after the start.":`从来没有挪动过任何东西，开始之后也没有再申请过内存。`,"O(1) for both operations, in a fixed block of memory. Used for audio, network packets and keyboard input.":`两种操作都是 O(1)，用的是一块固定的内存。用于音频、网络数据包和键盘输入。`},deques:s,"monotonic-stack":{"while the stack has a top smaller than x:":`当 栈顶比 x 小:`,"pop it: its answer is x":`弹出它：它的答案是 x`,"push x":`把 x 压入栈`,"whatever is left has no answer":`剩下的都没有答案`,"Where it has got to":`进行到哪里了`,"Next greater":`下一个更大的数`,"For every number in 5, 3, 2, 6, 4, 8, find the <strong>next greater</strong> one: the first bigger number that comes after it. For 5 that is 6. For 4 it is 8.":`对 5、3、2、6、4、8 中的每个数，找出<strong>下一个更大的数</strong>：在它后面出现的第一个比它大的数。5 的是 6。4 的是 8。`,"Checking each number against everything after it works, but that is O(n²). A stack does it in one pass.":`把每个数和它后面的所有数比较也行，但那是 O(n²)。用栈一趟就能完成。`,"Keep the numbers still waiting for an answer. A block here is as wide as its value is big.":`存放还在等答案的数。这里每个方块的宽度和它的值一样大。`,Answered:`已回答`,"Wait on the stack":`在栈上等待`,"5 has seen nothing bigger yet, because it has seen nothing at all. It goes on the stack to wait.":`5 还没见过更大的数，因为它什么都还没见过。它进栈等待。`,"The stack holds exactly the numbers that have no answer so far.":`栈里存的正好是目前还没有答案的数。`,"Smaller ones wait":`小的也等着`,"3 arrives. Is it the answer for 5? No, it is smaller. So 5 keeps waiting, and 3 starts waiting too, on top of it.":`3 来了。它是 5 的答案吗？不是，它更小。所以 5 继续等，3 也开始等，在 5 的上面。`,"Always in order":`始终有序`,Invariant:`不变量`,"2 is smaller again, so it waits as well. Look at the shape: every block is smaller than the one beneath it.":`2 又更小，所以它也等着。看看形状：每个方块都比它下面的小。`,"That is what <strong>monotonic</strong> means, and it is no accident. Anything that would break the order is dealt with before the new value goes on.":`这就是<strong>单调</strong>的意思，而且这不是巧合。任何会打乱顺序的东西，都会在新值进栈之前处理掉。`,"The smallest waiting value is always on top, so it is the first one a new value should be compared with.":`等待中的最小值总在顶上，所以新值总是先和它比较。`,"A bigger one arrives":`来了个更大的`,"6 is bigger than the top, 2. So 6 is what 2 was waiting for: pop it, with its answer. The same goes for 3, and then for 5.":`6 比栈顶的 2 大。所以 6 就是 2 在等的数：弹出 2，带着它的答案。3 也一样，然后是 5。`,"Three answers from one arrival. Then 6 itself goes on the stack to wait.":`一次到达，得到三个答案。然后 6 自己进栈等待。`,"And a smaller one":`再来个小的`,"4 is smaller than 6, so nothing is answered. It waits on top, and the stack is in order again.":`4 比 6 小，所以没有谁得到答案。它在顶上等着，栈又是有序的了。`,"Clear it again":`再清一次`,"8 is bigger than 4 and bigger than 6: both come off, both with the answer 8.":`8 比 4 大，也比 6 大：两个都出栈，答案都是 8。`,"Then 8 waits. It is the last value, so nothing is coming to answer it.":`然后 8 等待。它是最后一个值，所以不会再有谁来回答它了。`,"Whatever is still on the stack at the end never met anything bigger. 8 has no next greater value.":`到最后还留在栈里的，从没遇到过更大的数。8 没有下一个更大的数。`,"Every number was pushed once and popped once, however the pops were bunched together. That is 2n steps: <strong>O(n)</strong>.":`不管弹出是怎么扎堆的，每个数都只压入一次、弹出一次。一共 2n 步：<strong>O(n)</strong>。`,"Days until a warmer day, the span of a stock price, the largest rectangle in a histogram.":`离下一个更暖和的日子还有几天、股价的跨度、直方图中最大的矩形。`,"8 → none":`8 → 无`,"Six values, six pushes, six pops.":`六个值，六次压入，六次弹出。`},"monotonic-queue":{"for each x in a, at index i:":`对每个 a 中的 x，下标为 i:`,"while the back of the deque is smaller than x:":`当 双端队列的后端比 x 小:`,"pop it from the back      // it can never win now":`把它从后端弹出      // 它再也不可能胜出了`,"push x at the back":`把 x 压入后端`,"if the front has left the window: pop it from the front":`如果 前端已经离开窗口: 把它从前端弹出`,"once the window is full: the front is its maximum":`一旦窗口满了: 前端就是它的最大值`,Candidates:`候选`,"The biggest in every window":`每个窗口里最大的`,"Slide a window of three along this row and report the largest value in it each time.":`让一个三格的窗口沿着这一排滑动，每次报出其中最大的值。`,"Scanning each window afresh costs three looks per window. A deque that keeps only the values that could still win does it in one pass.":`每个窗口都重新扫描，每个窗口要看三次。用一个只保留还可能胜出的值的双端队列，一趟就能完成。`,Deque:`双端队列`,Maximums:`最大值`,"Keep the candidates":`保留候选`,"4 arrives: a candidate. 2 arrives. It is smaller than 4, but it is also newer, so it will outlast 4 in the window. It might be the maximum later. Keep both.":`4 来了：一个候选。2 来了。它比 4 小，但它也更新，所以它在窗口里会比 4 待得久。它以后可能是最大值。两个都留着。`,"smaller, but newer":`更小，但更新`,"Bigger and newer beats both":`又大又新，胜过两者`,"5 arrives. It is bigger than 2 and bigger than 4, and it will be in the window longer than either. Neither can ever be the maximum again: throw them out.":`5 来了。它比 2 大，也比 4 大，而且它在窗口里会比它们待得都久。它们俩再也不可能是最大值了：扔掉。`,"The window is full, and the front of the deque is its maximum: 5.":`窗口满了，双端队列的前端就是它的最大值：5。`,"Why “monotonic”":`为什么叫“单调”`,"What is left in the deque always runs from biggest to smallest.":`双端队列里剩下的，总是从大到小排列。`,"max = 5":`最大值 = 5`,"The window moves on and 1 arrives. It beats nothing, so it queues up behind 5. The maximum is still the front: 5.":`窗口往前移，1 来了。它谁也胜不过，所以排在 5 后面。最大值仍然是前端：5。`,"Out of the back":`从后端出去`,"3 arrives and knocks out 1, which is smaller and older. 5 is still inside the window, and still the maximum.":`3 来了，把 1 挤了出去，1 更小也更旧。5 仍在窗口里，仍是最大值。`,"6 arrives and clears the deque. 5 would have left anyway: the window has moved past it, and values that fall out of the window are dropped from the front.":`6 来了，清空了双端队列。5 反正也要走了：窗口已经越过了它，掉出窗口的值会从前端丢掉。`,"Every value entered the deque once and left it once.":`每个值都只进入双端队列一次、离开一次。`,"O(n) in total, whatever the window size.":`总共 O(n)，不管窗口多大。`,"max = 6":`最大值 = 6`}};export{n as arrays,c as default,s as deques,r as kmp,i as matrices,e as memory,o as queues,t as recursion,a as stacks};